fnOS Desktop Shell — vendored third-party resources

Upstream: https://github.com/aurysian-yan/fnOS_UI_Mods
Pinned commit: 483c3e2e217faebc1be45b4e824865854a61e3dd
License: FnOS UI Mods Non-Commercial License 1.0 (see LICENSE, copied verbatim below)

Packaging changes made by this project (upstream files themselves are UNMODIFIED):
  1. chrome.* compatibility shim injected ahead of content-script.js (inject/shim.js)
  2. chrome.runtime.getURL() reimplemented to return data: URLs instead of chrome-extension:// URLs
  3. mod.js delivered through the shim-provided data: URL, with a MutationObserver fallback that
     executes the unmodified original if the data: script is blocked by page CSP
  4. configuration is supplied by the host application instead of chrome.storage
  5. content-script.js is not evaluated as a top-level document-start script: its unmodified
     bytes are embedded in a generated wrapper (src-tauri/src/injector.rs) that runs them only
     once document.documentElement exists (MutationObserver on document, DOMContentLoaded
     fallback) and records a synchronous throw as window.__FNOS_UPSTREAM_ERROR__
  6. the upstream brand marks icons/icon{16,32,48,128}.png are used as this application's own
     icon: `cargo tauri icon` is run on the 128 px source to produce src-tauri/icons/icon.ico
     (multi-size) and src-tauri/icons/icon.png, and icons/icon32.png is embedded with
     include_bytes! as the tray icon. No upstream pixel is altered; tool-generated sizes above
     128 px are upscales of that same 128 px source (the largest size upstream ships).
  7. T14b: the settings window hosts the upstream popup UI (popup.html + popup.js) instead of
     this project's own hand-written settings groups. ui/settings/popup.js and every PNG it
     can name (prefect_icon/*.png, icons/*.png) are byte-identical copies; ui/settings/popup.html
     differs from the vendored popup.html by exactly ONE inserted line,
     `<script src="./chrome-shim.js"></script>` placed immediately before the popup.js script
     tag, because a chrome.* compatibility layer must define window.chrome before the popup
     runs. That shim (ui/settings/chrome-shim.js) is this project's own code: it reimplements
     chrome.storage.{sync,local} / chrome.tabs.* / chrome.runtime.* / chrome.action.* on top of
     the host application (get_config / set_config / get_page_state / get_page_report / the
     settings-only local store), neutralises the upstream update check (no network requests;
     this application pins the vendored commit) and refuses local font-file import, which this
     project does not implement (upstream popup.js itself is unmodified).

